In <Nov13.122359.34051@yuma.ACNS.ColoState.EDU> rubrduck@lamar.ColoState.EDU (Tamara Snyder) writes:

>Hello out there again...I am trying to get Nethack 3.1.3 up and running on
>my pc.  I thought i had Microsoft C ver 7.0, but i had turbo c ++ =(.
>Ive tried to locate MC7 but it has been discontinued...and replaced with
>visual C++ V 1.0.  Is the nethack source compatible with V C++? *sigh*

NetHack can be compiled with Visual C++ V1.0 as long as you have the
professional version.  The regular release (non-professional) won't
allow you to build MSDOS executables at all, only windows programs.
Once you have the professional version of Visual C++, you can use
the same steps and files that you would for MSC V7.0.

You should also read the Install.dos file before attempting to build
NetHack. It states (near the beginning):

I.  Dispelling the Myths:

    Compiling NetHack is not as easy as it sounds, nor as hard as it
    looks however it will behoove you to read this entire file through 
    before beginning the task.

    We have provided the proper makefiles for building NetHack using the
    following compilers:

    Microsoft C 6.0a
    Microsoft C 7.0 and Microsoft Visual C++ Professional (MSVC) 1.0
    DJGPP       1.9 or later

    For specific details concerning each compiler, please see the
    corresponding appendix.



